---
作者: Stefan
题目: Bug报告地点：/domains/std/wizroom...
日期: Tue Mar  3 07:08:34 1998
I understand that people are adding colorful names, descriptions, etc...
But, please note that color code also can cause trouble.
e.g:
你身上带着：
  一件玲珑细环甲(jia)
  七十两银子(silver)
  一百九十九两金子(gold)
  一件藤甲(teng jia)
but:
wear 玲珑细环甲
这里没有玲珑细环甲。

Then I looked into the code:
set_id("jia", HIG+"玲珑细环甲"+NOR);

So, I could never "wear 玲珑细环甲" because I can not input the
color code myself on the input line. This kind of word parsing
feature becomes useless when color code is used. 

command parsing normally involves adjectives ids. If I have a
细环甲, and adjective is 玲珑, I can either wear 细环甲, or
wear 玲珑细环甲. Or even, wear 玲珑jia. If there are color
code in between, it'll cause trouble.

Another thing is that color was designed to be able to be turned
off when the user prefers non-color mode. Hard coded color as
the above will not make this to happen. 



